ong></p><ul><li><p>You bring <strong>1-4 years</strong> experience in B2B SaaS Sales.</p></li><li><p>You are a passionate sales talent with a hunter mentality, who is driven to succeed by building valuable and long-lasting customer relationships.</p></li><li><p>You have excellent communication skills, both verbal and written, in German and English. Any additional language is an advantage</p></li><li><p>You have a proven track record of overachievement and hitting sales targets.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>The perks of working with us:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Build and expand your network in our exciting customer portfolio with global brands like Phillips, Samsung, Bosch, Adidas, and many more.</p></li><li><p>Report directly to the Chief Sales Officer - quick decision making and flat hierarchy.</p></li><li><p>Competitive base salary and a motivating, uncapped commission plan to celebrate your successes, approx 100-120k OTE.</p></li><li><p>30 vacation days, plus 30 workation days / year within the EU.</p></li><li><p>Enjoy perks like corporate benefits, Urban Sports and Deutschland ticket subsidies.</p></li><li><p>Regular company celebrations and team events!</p></li><li><p>Join a passionate international team of 25+ nationalities!</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/demoup-cliplister/account-executive-german-speaking-berlin-361361","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Berlin, Berlin, Germany","created_at":1794239491},{"slug":"financial-analyst-berlin-59313","company_name":"Taxfix","title":"Financial Analyst (d/w/m)","description":"<h2>Our story:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every year millions of people are either filing their taxes in fear or giving up on their tax refund altogether. We're working on fixing that. Our intuitive app enables anyone, regardless of education or background, to file their taxes with newfound confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spread across Germany, Spain and the UK, the team at Taxfix Group with its brands Taxfix and Steuerbot, is a compassionate group of solution-finders. We speak our minds openly, and with over 400 professionals, including tax experts, developers, and IT security experts, we're rich in ideas and voices. The group has facilitated more than 3.5 billion euros in tax refunds for its customers since its founding in 2016.<br /></p><h2><strong>Your challenge</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Financial Analyst, Planning &amp; Reporting Systems, you will build and maintain our planning and reporting models and dashboards, make sure data flows correctly from our source systems, and ensure the numbers the business relies on are accurate and consistent.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alongside this, you will support core FP&amp;A work such as forecasting, variance analysis and month-end reporting. The role reports to the Senior Director of FP&amp;A and works closely with FinOps, Data and business stakeholders.</p><h2><br /><strong>Your responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain models in our planning platform, including dimensions, hierarchies and mapping tables, in line with the agreed model design</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build product P&amp;Ls and product dashboards, and prepare the monthly reviews with commercial product owners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor data flows from our ERP, HR and other source systems into the planning platform, and resolve issues together with FinOps and Data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run monthly reconciliations between the planning platform, the general ledger and reported figures, and document the checks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the transition of planning and reporting workflows into the planning platform, in close collaboration with the FP&amp;A team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support FinOps on the interface between planning and consolidation, so management and statutory views reconcile</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain access rights, version control and model documentation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support and train budget owners in using the platform for their planning and reporting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate recurring reports and workflows, using AI tools where they remove manual work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support core FP&amp;A processes when needed: monthly reporting, forecast updates, variance analysis and management materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver ad-hoc analysis on product performance to support commercial decisions</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience in FP&amp;A, controlling, finance systems or a similar analytical finance role, ideally in a fast-growing or subscription-based business; alternatively, a background as implementation consultant for Pigment, Anaplan or similar planning tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building models or reports in a modern planning tool (e.g. Pigment, Anaplan, Adaptive); Pigment experience is highly valued</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of financial statements and accounting principles, with hands-on experience in budgeting, forecasting and variance analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Excel skills and working knowledge of SQL; experience with ERP, consolidation or BI tools (e.g. NetSuite, LucaNet, Looker) is a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High attention to detail and care for data quality: you notice when a number does not tie, and you find out why</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on use of AI in finance work (e.g. LLM assistants, AI features in finance and planning tools), and the curiosity to adopt new tools as they mature</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communicator, able to explain numbers to non-finance stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structured, independent and pragmatic, with a strong sense of ownership<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Why Taxfix? </h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A chance to do meaningful, people-centric work with an international team of passionate professionals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holistic well-being with free mental health coaching sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A monthly allowance to spend on an extensive range of services that you can use and roll over as flexibly as you like.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee stock options for all employees—because everyone deserves to benefit from the success they help to create.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 annual vacation days and flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A generous learning budget to support your personal and professional development and guidance from our internal L&amp;D experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from abroad for up to six weeks every year. Just align with your team, and then enjoy your trip.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plenty of opportunities to socialise as a team. In addition to internal meetups, our international team hosts regular get-togethers—virtually and in person when possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free tax declaration filing, of course, through the Taxfix app—and internal support for all personal tax-related questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a four-legged friend in your life? We’re happy to have dogs join us in the office.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Excited? So are we. Check out our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/taxfix/life/8684512c-424f-44de-8d07-6e6b516e3319/?viewAsMember=true"> <u>Life at Taxfix</u></a> page on LinkedIn to get a glimpse of our culture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Taxfix, we believe that incredible things happen when you have a wealth of perspectives and experiences. We're proudly committed to equal employment and development opportunities no matter your gender, race, religion, age, sexual orientation, colour, disability, or place of origin. To help mitigate any potential unconscious biases, we ask that you refrain from including your picture, age, or marital status on your CV. Let your experiences speak for themselves.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not sure if you meet all the requirements for this role? Please apply anyway. You might bring something special to the team that we hadn't considered previously.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/taxfix/financial-analyst-berlin-59313","tags":["FP&A"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1794238813},{"slug":"rust-engineer-berlin-6108","company_name":"Deepslate","title":"Rust Engineer (m/f/d)","description":"<h1>Rust Engineer</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Berlin and surrounding</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Deepslate, we are building Speech to Speech Voice AI models that sound and act indistinguishably from a human. And we believe everyone should be able to use them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With its endless languages, dialects, accents, subtle intonations, and speech melodies, <strong>voice</strong> remains a highly complex unsolved frontier.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That is exactly why we started Deepslate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top-tier investors from the Tech and AI sectors, as well as a major German VC fund, we are incredibly well-funded and moving fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We are building the future of communication.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aren't trying to build another standalone platform; instead, we are the intelligence engine powering countless other applications. Whether it's integrated as a module by a CRM provider, plugged into another Voice AI platform, or directly embedded into an enterprise system by our integration partners, our model is built to work wherever it is needed.</p><h2>Your Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Many core parts of our model stack are written in Rust. At the heart of it is our inference engine, written entirely in Rust.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your mission is to build and improve these systems. You will work on the inference engine, take ownership of other Rust projects, and help decide how everything fits together. We need someone who enjoys writing good Rust code and can design software that stays understandable and maintainable as it grows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our models need to respond in real time. The software you build will directly influence how fast and reliable they are in an actual conversation.</p><h3>What You'll Do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build in Rust:</strong> Develop our inference engine and other core components of the model stack. Take projects from the first architectural decisions to running in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design the Architecture:</strong> Decide how components and services communicate, where responsibilities belong, and how we can extend the system without making it harder to work on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work on Real-Time Systems:</strong> Build async Rust systems that handle concurrent workloads and streaming audio with low latency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve Performance:</strong> Find bottlenecks, understand what's causing them, and improve latency, throughput, and resource usage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Write Production-Ready Code:</strong> Build software that we can test, debug, and operate reliably. Help improve our tooling, documentation, and development practices along the way.</p></li></ul><h3>What We're Looking For: Must-Haves</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands-on experience with <strong>Rust</strong>, including ownership, borrowing, composition, and idiomatic Rust design patterns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid experience with <strong>async Rust</strong>. You know how to structure concurrent applications and deal with synchronization, cancellation, and backpressure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and working with <strong>microservice architectures</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A true startup mindset:</strong> You are comfortable navigating the glorious chaos of an early-stage codebase. Inconsistent structures, missing docs. You name it, you'll help fix it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive and Vision:</strong> You aren't just looking to blindly process Jira tickets. You want to actively shape the product, architect solutions, and take complete project ownership.</p></li></ul><h3>Ideally, You Also Bring</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of <strong>actor systems</strong> and experience using actors to structure concurrent applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with <strong>real-time systems</strong>, whether in embedded environments or the cloud. Both are relevant to us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with <strong>C/C++ interoperability</strong>, including generating Rust bindings with <strong>bindgen</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>German</strong>, spoken and written.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice-to-Haves</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with <strong>CUDA or GPU computing</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributions to <strong>open-source projects</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Python</strong> knowledge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with lower-level performance engineering, such as debugging memory leaks or understanding performance at the machine instruction level.</p></li></ul><h3>What We Offer</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Ownership:</strong> Our Rust stack is central to the company. You'll have the trust and freedom to make architectural decisions and see them through.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>True R&amp;D Freedom:</strong> We give you the time, resources, and trust to research and build technology that simply doesn't exist yet. There are difficult problems here, and room to try different approaches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive Compensation:</strong> We are well-funded by top-tier VCs. We offer a highly competitive salary. We are looking for top talent, and we are ready to pay for it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Serious Compute:</strong> You will have access to the hardware and cloud infrastructure necessary to build, test, and optimize the systems running our models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deepslate is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates regardless of gender, nationality, ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, or sexual orientation.</p><hr><p>Compensation: €75K – €120K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • €75K – €120K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/deepslate/rust-engineer-berlin-6108","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1794238812},{"slug":"tech-recruiter-all-genders-munchen-411368","company_name":"Wemolo","title":"Tech Recruiter (all genders)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Talent Acquisition ist für uns mehr als Recruiting. Wir verstehen es als eine echte Disziplin, die sich stetig weiterentwickelt durch neue Technologien, neue Ansätze und vor allem durch die Menschen, die sie gestalten. Dabei zählt für uns nicht nur das Ergebnis, sondern auch der Weg dorthin. Und genau diesen Anspruch wollen wir mit dir weiterentwickeln.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als <strong>Tech Recruiter (all genders)</strong> übernimmst du die End-to-end-Verantwortung für unsere Product- und Engineering-Rollen – von Software Engineering über Engineering Management, Data und Plattform bis hin zu Product Management. Du bringst nicht nur deine Erfahrung im Tech Recruiting mit, sondern auch dein technisches Verständnis in unser Talent-Team ein und hilfst uns, als Team in diesem Bereich zu wachsen. Wir haben bereits einen standardisierten Hiring-Prozess, du gestaltest ihn mit deinem Tech-Recruiting-Know-how aktiv weiter.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dabei unterstützt dich ein modernes, AI-gestütztes Setup mit Ashby als ATS, Metaview als AI-Notetaker sowie Claude, Notion und Gemini. Die Technologie nimmt dir dabei nicht das Recruiting ab, sie gibt dir mehr Raum für das, worauf es wirklich ankommt: die richtigen Tech-Talente zu verstehen, zu gewinnen und gemeinsam die besten Matches zu schaffen.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What to expect</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-end Recruiting: </strong>Du übernimmst die Verantwortung für den gesamten Recruiting-Prozess unserer Product- und Engineering-Rollen, vom Hiring Kick-off und Talent Mapping bis hin zur Vertragsunterzeichnung</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sparring Partner: </strong>Du bist ein vertrauenswürdiger Partner für unsere Engineering- und Product-Hiring-Manager, forderst sie heraus und bringst dein Tech-Markt-Know-how aktiv in die Entscheidungsfindung ein</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pipeline Building: </strong>Du sprichst gezielt Tech-Talente über verschiedene Kanäle an und baust nachhaltige Talentpools durch Active Sourcing und Employer Branding Initiativen auf</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data &amp; Analytics: </strong>Deine Pipeline baust du basierend auf fundierten Daten und nutzt diese auch aktiv in der Hiring Manager Beratung</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team-Impact: </strong>Du bringst dein Tech-Recruiting-Know-how ins Team ein, teilst dein Wissen zu Rollenprofilen und Marktgegebenheiten und hilfst uns, unser Verständnis für Tech-Hiring kontinuierlich zu schärfen</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Inspire us by</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Background: </strong>Abgeschlossenes Studium und 3–5 Jahre Erfahrung im Tech Recruiting (z. B. SWE, Data, Platform, Product) in einem dynamischen Umfeld</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expertise: </strong>Sehr gute Fachkenntnisse im In-house Tech Recruiting, Erfahrung in der Einstellung von Entry-Level bis Senior-Positionen über verschiedene technische Disziplinen hinweg</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder Management: </strong>Erfahrung in der Zusammenarbeit mit Engineering- und Product-Führungskräften und der Entwicklung langfristiger Talentstrategien durch Talentpools, Employer Branding Aktivitäten und innovative Talent Acquisition Ansätze</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data-driven: </st