to vulgar, violent, and sexual content.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investigate and take action on member reports and proactive detections involving safety concerns, including harassment, threats, non-consensual imagery, and other potential violations of Bumble Inc.’s Community Guidelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide thoughtful, high-touch and trauma-informed support to members who have experienced safety incidents, demonstrating Respect and care while following established safety processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review accounts and content flagged for potential safety violations, applying policies and operational guidance consistently while using sound judgment to determine appropriate next steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage sensitive and time-critical cases with attention to detail, taking ownership of your work and seeing cases through from initial review to an appropriate outcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate purposefully with Trust &amp; Safety, Customer Experience, Legal, and other partners to escalate and help resolve cases that require additional expertise or support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify recurring issues, patterns, and opportunities to improve workflows, sharing insights that can strengthen operational consistency and member safety.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI-supported tools and internal systems to improve efficiency and support decision-making, reviewing outputs critically for accuracy, bias, privacy, and fairness and applying human judgment before taking action.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in on-call rotations, including evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed, adapting with an agile mindset to support our global community.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Requires 1+ years of experience, though we welcome candidates with alternative backgrounds that demonstrate equivalent skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring experience in Trust &amp; Safety, customer support, crisis response, content moderation, or another environment where you have handled sensitive or safety-related issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable reviewing potentially distressing content, including material relating to child exploitation, sexual or physical violence, suicide and self-harm, while approaching this work with care and professionalism.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate clearly and compassionately in writing and verbally, particularly when supporting vulnerable individuals or navigating sensitive situations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply sound judgment within established policies and processes, balancing efficiency with careful, consistent decision-making and demonstrating Bumble’s values of Respect and Excellence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate purposefully with colleagues, take ownership of your work, and maintain an agile mindset as priorities, cases, and operational needs evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in Spanish, Portuguese, French, or another language in addition to English is welcomed but not required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bumble Inc. is the parent company of Bumble Date, BFF, and Badoo. The Bumble platform enables people to build healthy and equitable relationships, through Kind Connections. Founded by Whitney Wolfe Herd in 2014, Bumble was one of the first dating apps built with women at the center and connects people across dating (Bumble Date) and friendship (BFF). BFF is a friendship app where people in all stages of life can meet people nearby and create meaningful platonic connections and community based on shared interests. Badoo, which was founded in 2006, is one of the pioneers of web and mobile dating products.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI Fluency</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is important to us. We’re excited by people who are curious and experimental, and who think thoughtfully about how AI can amplify their impact and outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We encourage you to use AI responsibly as you prepare your application. Please don’t use it to fabricate experiences or answer questions live in interviews. We care deeply about authenticity and want to understand your real skills, judgment and voice, because building a meaningful, genuine connection with you matters to us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Compensation</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Will be determined based on factors such as the selected candidate’s qualifications, relevant experience, skill set, and other job-related considerations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Inclusion at Bumble Inc.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bumble Inc. is an equal opportunity employer and we strongly encourage people of all ages, color, lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, queer and non-binary people, veterans, parents, people with disabilities, and neurodivergent people to apply. We're happy to make any reasonable adjustments that will help you feel more confident throughout the process, please don't hesitate to let us know how we can help.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your application, please feel free to note which pronouns you use (For example: she/her, he/him, they/them, etc).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI in Bumble Inc. Hiring</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Bumble, we may use AI tools to support parts of our recruitment process — such as helping us record, transcribe, and summarize conversations, and supporting job alignment by comparing resumes and job descriptions to highlight skills and potential roles that may be a good match. These tools help us work more efficiently and stay focused on you during our conversations. Importantly, all hiring decisions are made by people. AI is used only to support our team’s efficiency and improve the candidate experience — not to evaluate or decide on your candidacy. Participation in AI-supported interviews and conversations is completely voluntary and will not impact your candidacy. If you’d prefer to opt out, simply let your recruiter or interviewer know at the start of a call, or anytime during the interview or conversation. Summaries and related data are retained only as long as needed in line with our internal data retention policies. If at any point you’d like a transcription or summary deleted, please contact your recruiter directly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fraudulent Candidate Detection</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our applicant tracking system analyzes signals relating to device, IP, email, and phone data associated with each application to protect applicants and our hiring process from fraudulent applications. These signals provide indicators for internal review only and do not constitute a definitive determination of identity or intent. No applicant is rejected, advanced, or otherwise affected based solely on this analysis without human review</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For further information on how we hold and manage your data, please refer to our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://bumble.com/en/candidate-privacy-policy"> Privacy Policy</a>.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bumble-inc/integrity-operations-specialist-london-288787","tags":["Customer Experience & Trust"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"UK London","created_at":1794228016},{"slug":"regional-sales-director-enterprise-uk-england-312844","company_name":"Kong","title":"Regional Sales Director, Enterprise - UK","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Are you ready to unlock intelligence?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don’t think you meet all of the criteria below but are still interested in the job, please apply.  Nobody checks every box - we’re looking for candidates that are particularly strong in a few areas, and have some interest and capabilities in others.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role: </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kong is seeking an Enterprise Sales Leader to help us build and grow the Kong API platform and our Enterprise Sales Team in the UK. We are searching for a seasoned industry leader who will lead our Enterprise Account Executives and drive business results and revenue. Reporting to the VP of Northern EMEA, this senior leadership position will have ownership and accountability to ensure Kong maximises our market potential bringing in new customers as well as growing our existing clients. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This leader will work closely with our other senior leaders to ensure decisions are driving the overall Kong business goals and our long term vision continues to thrive. You will play a part in reshaping and leading the incredible growth of Kong. It is the intention of the leadership team to build a high quality, sustainable and strong sales organization. To date, a significant amount of Kong’s success has been gained through the quality of our product, our global account base, our adoption by the open source community and by inbound leads. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will build and strengthen a quality, scalable, regional sales team focused on acquisition of new brands and targeted account plans. Kong is the perfect environment for you to have a significant impact and grow our amazing company. We are a people first organisation and expect you to be the same.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growing Kong’s presence and footprint in Enterprise accounts in the UK.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driving a highly performant and highly accountable culture to achieve and exceed sales goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attract, hire and retain top talent through your network and in collaboration with the rest of the org.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide strong coaching and mentorship on the sales process, PG, qualification and closing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct weekly forecast meetings with your team and report to leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate effectively with Marketing, Partners, and all stakeholders.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have been a top performer as an IC and front-line manager with a track record of overachievement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accurate forecasting at the individual and team levels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to recruit, develop, and retain top talent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong territory management at a regional level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven systems/methodology for consistent pipeline generation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using and teaching sales methodologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Energy, passion, and rigour in your career as a Sales leader.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Kong:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kong Inc., the AI Connectivity Company, is building the connectivity layer of AI. Trusted by the Fortune 500® and AI-native startups alike, Kong’s unified API and AI platform enables organizations to secure, manage, accelerate, govern, and monetize the flow of intelligence across APIs and AI traffic — on any model, any cloud. For more information, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.konghq.com">www.konghq.com</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/kong/regional-sales-director-enterprise-uk-england-312844","tags":["All Cost Center"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"England, United Kingdom","created_at":1794228015},{"slug":"senior-data-engineer-storage-messaging-headquarters-117527","company_name":"Bitvavo","title":"Senior Data Engineer - Storage & Messaging","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">In 2018, Bitvavo launched the first version of its digital assets trading platform, to bridge the gap between traditional currencies and digital assets. By offering transparent fees, a wide range of assets and an easy to use platform, Bitvavo is making the currency of the future accessible for everyone.<br /><br />In two years' time, Bitvavo has established itself as the market leader in the Netherlands and one of the largest in Europe, with over one million users exchanging tens of billions of digital assets a year.</p><h2><strong>About the Opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a talented Senior Data Platform Engineer to join the Storage and Messaging team in our established Platform Engineering team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an exchange. System scalability, performance and engineering productivity matter in everything that we do. Our platform domain is committed to fostering autonomy by providing engineering teams with paved paths to develop robust, secure, compliant, and scalable systems. We're seeking exceptional talent to join us in making this a reality<br /></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a self-service platform that empowers teams to build at scale across diverse database and messaging technologies, enabling the seamless and reliable development of application and data products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously evolve our platform to support new data models and use cases, including structured and semi-structured data models, stream processing, and data governance at scale .</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a secure, scalable, and compliant data infrastructure using Infrastructure as Code and automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enable data ingestion, processing, and consumption at scale. All are offered entirely as self-service.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor teammates by sharing technical knowledge, providing constructive feedback, and driving engineering excellence.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Look For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with one or more programming languages. We primarily use Golang and Python (Java is a plus), but we value problem-solving ability over syntax familiarity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of platform engineering principles and distributed data systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with SQL and No-SQL databases. Understanding of data warehousing and batch/stream processing is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with distributed messaging systems such as Kafka, including cluster operations, topic/partition design, consumer group tuning, schema registry, and stream processing with Flink</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in using infrastructure as code tools (like Terraform) and container orchestration platforms (like Kubernetes) in a cloud-first environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional communication skills. We expect engineers to take ownership of their work end-to-end and communicate directly with stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High sense of ownership, accountability and engineering mindset. We value engineers who take initiative and advocate for the long-term health of our data ecosystem.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We care more about your engineering mindset than your knowledge of any specific tool or technology. If this sounds exciting, even if you do not check every box, let's talk!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Bitvavo, we believe that diverse perspectives drive innovation, foster creativity, and lead to better outcomes. We are committed to building a team that reflects the diversity of the communities we serve and creating an inclusive environment where everyone can thrive. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Regardless of race, ethnicity, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, ability, or any other characteristic. Join us and be part of a team that values and celebrates your unique contributions.<br /><br />Bitvavo does not accept resumes from staffing, search, or recruitment firms without a signed agreement. If you send us a resume without such an agreement, we may contact the candidate directly without any obligation whatsoever and no fee of any kind will be paid should we hire the candidate.</em></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Bitvavo, we believe in attracting, motivating and retaining talented people through market-competitive offerings that go beyond compensation alone. To learn more about our total rewards package and the benefits we offer, visit our Life at Bitvavo page.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bitvavo/senior-data-engineer-storage-messaging-headquarters-117527","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Headquarters","created_at":1794228015},{"slug":"senior-devops-engineer-london-196554","company_name":"Xyz Reality","title":"Senior DevOps Engineer","description":"<h2>Build the infrastructure powering the future of construction</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.xyzreality.com">XYZ Reality</a>, we’ve created the world’s first engineering-grade Augmented Reality solution for construction. Our technology, The Atom, is used on major projects worldwide to help construction teams build more accurately, efficiently and with fewer mistakes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Series B business scaling across the UK, US and Europe, the infrastructure behind our technology needs to scale with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Senior DevOps Engineer to take ownership of the cloud infrastructure and DevOps practices powering our BIM Platform, working across cloud, container and CI/CD platforms, observability, security and developer tooling.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on senior engineering role with broad ownership across our cloud and platform infrastructure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work closely with our Engineering, Data and Security teams to build reliable, scalable infrastructure while improving how our developers deploy, monitor and troubleshoot their services.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want DevOps to be an enabler rather than a gatekeeper. That means building the tooling, automation and self-service capabilities that allow engineering teams to move quickly and safely without creating unnecessary dependencies on DevOps. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll have the autonomy to identify where our infrastructure and engineering practices can improve and take ownership of making those improvements happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role is based in our London office on a hybrid basis, with 3 days per week in the office. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You’ll Be Doing</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architect, maintain and evolve our cloud infrastructure and container platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain Infrastructure-as-Code and configuration management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and improve CI/CD pipelines for fast, safe and repeatable deployments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build observability across infrastructure and services: monitoring, logging, alerting and distributed tracing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve reliability, scalability and performance through capacity planning, autoscaling and resource optimisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own resilience, including backup, recovery and failover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own infrastructure security across our platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evolve incident response, on-call practices, runbooks and blameless post-mortems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with our Data team to support reliable, scalable relational and document databases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build self-service tooling, templates and documentation that reduce reliance on DevOps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support infrastructure for data pipelines and AI/ML model deployment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner directly with developers on deployment, troubleshooting and infrastructure best practices.</p></li></ul><h2>What We’re Looking For</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a strong, hands-on DevOps Engineer who is comfortable owning complex infrastructure and operating across a broad technical environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll ideally have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrable in-depth experience in DevOps, Infrastructure or Cloud Engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands-on experience with a major public cloud (Azure, AWS or GCP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep experience running container orchestration platforms in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Infrastructure-as-Code experience with modern tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing and operating CI/CD pipelines (e.g. GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Azure DevOps).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience with containers and Docker.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with monitoring, logging, alerting and observability in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good knowledge of infrastructure security best practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building automation in Python, Go, Bash or TypeScript.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong troubleshooting skills and ownership of production infrastructure and incidents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to make pragmatic decisions and explain infrastructure trade-offs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with high-availability infrastructure, relational or document databases, AI/ML infrastructure, ETL/data pipelines, FinOps or certified/regulated environments would be a bonus.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Above all, we’re looking for someone who enjoys automating away problems rather than repeatedly solving them manually. You’ll be comfortable taking ownership, challenging processes that don’t scale and building the tools and practices that make the wider engineering team more effective.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why Join Us</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Join a Series B business at an exciting stage of international growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏠 Hybrid working from our London office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏝️ 25 days annual leave + public holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Private healthcare with Vitality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎄 Additional Christmas shutdown days</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🪙 Biannual salary reviews</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥳 Summer &amp; Christmas company events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🍣 Free Thursday lunch and after-work gatherings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Employee referral scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚲 Cycle to Work scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌍 Make a real-world impact revolutionising the construction industry</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re a Senior DevOps Engineer who enjoys taking ownership, solving complex infrastructure challenges and building environments that enable engineering teams to move faster, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you'd like to see the products and technology we have created so far on our journey you can view it in action through our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/@XYZReality/videos">YouTube</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.xyzreality.com/">Website</a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/xyz-reality/senior-devops-engineer-london-196554","tags":["Platform"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office","created_at":1794228014},{"slug":"principal-compliance-associate-market-surveillance-london-235877","company_name":"Kraken","title":"Principal Compliance Associate - Market Surveillance","description":"<h1><strong>Building the Future of Open Finance</strong><br /></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payward - the parent company behind Kraken, NinjaTrader, Breakout,  xStocks, Payward Services and CF Benchmarks - has spent the last 15 years building one of the most modern and globally accessible financial infrastructure platforms in the industry, built to advance an open, global financial system.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2011, Kraken is one of the world's longest-standing crypto platforms, trusted by over 10 million individuals and institutions across the globe. It offers spot trading, margin, futures, staking, and OTC services, with products built for both individual investors and institutional clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kraken's Market Surveillance function is responsible for detecting, investigating and reporting market abuse across our regulated trading venues, spanning spot crypto markets, crypto futures, tokenised equities, OTC markets, and consumer trading. As our licensing footprint and product range grow, so does the scale and complexity of the surveillance programme behind them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring a Principal Compliance Associate to take on the function's most complex casework, and help shape how we detect and cover market abuse as the business scales.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>The opportunity</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own complex investigations end to end, writing findings up to a standard a regulator can rely on, and present conclusions to a range of stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead or contribute to periodic threshold and model reviews, recalibrating surveillance rules and alert thresholds as trading behaviour, products and market structure evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the design, build-out and integration of surveillance platform capability, including onboarding new products, venues and data sources onto the surveillance system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to market abuse risk assessments, helping identify and score risk across products, jurisdictions and entities, and translate findings into surveillance coverage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI and automation tools responsibly to speed up evidence-gathering, case reconstruction and detection-model development, always with human judgement over the final call.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support conflicts of interest, information barrier, and personal account dealing matters across Markets Compliance, extending beyond surveillance casework where buy-side or asset management experience is directly relevant.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience investigating market abuse or trading conduct inside a firm subject to market conduct regulation, such as an exchange, broker-dealer, trading venue, or comparable regulated trading business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record running investigations end to end, including writing findings up to a standard a regulator can rely on and presenting conclusions to stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of core market abuse typologies e.g. spoofing, wash trading, insider trading, front running, ramping.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with, or strong working knowledge of, threshold and model calibration, surveillance platform integration, market abuse risk assessments, and audit remediation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort using generative AI and other automation tools to improve the speed and quality of investigative work, while maintaining the human oversight regulated casework requires.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with a surveillance platform (such as Scila, Nasdaq SMARTS, Eventus, or NICE Actimize) and comfort with SQL or a similar query tool for evidence-gathering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, evidence-first written communication - your case files, escalations and regulatory drafts will sometimes be read by auditors and regulators without you in the room to explain them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to crypto-asset markets is welcomed but not required. What matters most is regulated-market investigation experience; strong candidates from traditional securities or derivatives markets are encouraged to apply.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">E-comms surveillance experience.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Unless a specific application deadline is stated in the job posting, applications are accepted on an ongoing basis.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Please note, applicants are permitted to redact or remove information on their resume that identifies age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We consider qualified applicants with criminal histories for employment on our team, assessing candidates in a manner consistent with the requirements of the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Our commitment</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payward is powered by people from around the world and we celebrate the diverse talents, backgrounds, contributions, and unique perspectives that everyone brings to the table. We hire based on merit, seeking out people with the right abilities, knowledge, and skills for the job. We encourage you to apply for roles where you don't fully meet the listed requirements, especially if you're passionate or knowledgeable about crypto.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We may ask candidates to complete job-related skills or work-style assessments as part of our hiring process. These assessments evaluate competencies relevant to the role and are applied consistently across candidates for similar positions. Results are considered alongside experience and interviews, and are not the sole basis for any employment decision.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an equal opportunity employer, we don't tolerate discrimination or harassment of any kind, whether based on race, ethnicity, age, gender identity, citizenship, religion, sexual orientation, disability, pregnancy, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay connected</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://twitter.com/krakenfx"><u>Follow us on Twitter</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://blog.kraken.com/#:~:text=Enter%20your%20email%20address"><u>Learn on the Kraken Blog</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/kraken-exchange/"><u>Connect on LinkedIn</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.kraken.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice"><u>Candidate Privacy Notice</u></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/kraken/principal-compliance-associate-market-surveillance-london-235877","tags":["Compliance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1794228014},{"slug":"product-engineer-london-213487","company_name":"Adclear","title":"Product Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Adclear</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Adclear, we’re building the trust layer for how the world’s most regulated companies bring products to market. Every bank, lender and investment platform runs into the same invisible pain: compliance review slows down every campaign, every launch, every idea. We’re turning the function that has always said “no” into infrastructure that says “yes, and here’s how.”</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a fundamental shift in how regulated industries and compliance teams operate, and we’re only at the beginning. The product you’ll help build is what people actually touch when they experience that shift.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2024, we’ve already earned the trust of leading innovators and established enterprises including Monzo, NatWest, PensionBee, Kraken, Coinbase and many others. Our early traction let us raise £2.6m in funding, and we’re now scaling fast. We’re building the product engine that turns a genuinely novel category into something people love to use, and this is where you come in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-stack product engineering role for someone who has shipped real features and wants to take on more ownership. You’ll work alongside senior engineers and the founders on product slices from spec to production. Over time you’ll own them end-to-end. Here’s the kind of work you’ll contribute to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Chrome extension that runs compliance checks inline in Google Docs, where marketers actually write copy. It was built with Monzo as the design partner and is public on the Chrome Web Store.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A natural-language copilot for compliance work. Users ask in plain English, the platform proposes typed actions, a human approves, and the action runs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The interface where reviewers watch the model reason through a decision, step in when they disagree, and feed structured corrections back into the rules.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrations that reach into wherever customers create marketing: Canva, Figma, Google Docs, Contentful, Workfront, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Monday.com">Monday.com</a>, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Frame.io">Frame.io</a> for video.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A dashboard that takes a long, unsorted list of compliance tasks and turns it into a single prioritised queue.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our users are compliance and marketing teams at leading fintechs. They use Adclear every day and tell us quickly when something’s wrong. That tight feedback loop is one of the best things about the job, and it’s a fast way to grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship product features from spec to production. Most of the work is across the full stack, and integration work where needed. You’ll start with guidance and take on bigger slices as you grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the surfaces compliance reviewers live in: workflows, review UIs, and the moments where model output meets human judgement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on features where AI is in the critical path. The model is genuinely part of the product, not bolted on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship a change to production on your first day and a feature in your first few weeks. We deploy continuously, so you’ll feel the pace immediately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring your perspective to what we build and how we build it. We want to hear when something doesn’t make sense.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn from senior engineers through code review, pairing and design discussions, and help raise the bar yourself.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven delivery.</strong> Building production web applications, with features you’ve shipped that real users depend on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growing ownership.</strong> You can take a well-scoped feature and run with it. You know when to ask for input and when to unblock yourself. You want to grow towards owning larger, more ambiguous pieces of work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product sense.</strong> You care about the user experience, notice when something feels off, and aren’t afraid to say so. You’re learning to balance polish against shipping at pace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration.</strong> You communicate clearly with engineers, designers and founders, ask good questions when something is underspecified, and are receptive to feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI literacy.</strong> You use modern coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, agents) day to day. You treat them as collaborators, check their output critically, and are curious about where they help and where they get in the way.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical skills</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid TypeScript and React, with working experience on the backend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with, or a strong interest in, building products where AI is in the critical path.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with modern web tooling, including Node and Postgres.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Cloudflare Workers, Hono or Drizzle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to regulated industries such as fintech, healthtech or legaltech.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Stack</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">React, TypeScript and Tailwind on the frontend. A Hono API on Cloudflare Workers. Drizzle and Postgres on the data layer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Compensation</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meaningful equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private healthcare and dental</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hardware budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monthly gym contribution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional development budget</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/adclear/product-engineer-london-213487","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794228014},{"slug":"strategic-account-executive-middle-east-392674","company_name":"Pingidentity","title":"Strategic Account Executive (Middle East)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ping Identity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ping Identity, we believe in making digital experiences both secure and seamless for all users, without compromise. We call this digital freedom. And it&#39;s not just something we provide our customers. It&#39;s something that inspires our company. People don&#39;t come here to join a culture that&#39;s built on digital freedom. They come to cultivate it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our intelligent, cloud identity platform lets people shop, work, bank, and interact wherever and however they want. Without friction. Without fear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While protecting digital identities is at the core of our technology, protecting individual identities is at the core of our culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/championing-every-identity.html&quot;&gt;We champion every identity.&lt;/a&gt; One of our core values, Respect Individuality, reminds us to celebrate differences so you are empowered to bring your authentic self to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re headquartered in Denver, Colorado and we have offices and employees around the globe. We serve the largest, most demanding enterprises worldwide, including more than half of the Fortune 100. At Ping Identity, we&#39;re changing the way people and businesses think about cybersecurity, digital experiences, and identity and access management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The Strategic Account Executive is a field-based position with ownership of an assigned territory in the Middle East region focused on net new logo opportunities. You will have the ability to utilize a robust internal resource model, a broad tech stack, and a global partner directory to position yourself for future success.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We will consider applicants based in the UK or France only&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, implement, measure and review a personal plan that drives achievement of performance goals aligned to the regional sales strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position and articulate our value proposition to customers to maximize the business opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and close complex contracts with the support of global partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on sales activity and forecasts to senior management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare indicative subscription pricing and customer offers, including reviewing broader opportunities such as training and professional services modules, and guides request for proposal responses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides customer feedback to marketing, customer success, product management, and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively to acquire additional/specialist resources as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years&amp;nbsp;quota-carrying experience selling enterprise software solutions,&amp;nbsp;preferably IAM or cybersecurity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable, successful experience of selling in the&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;collapsed-field-text&quot;&gt;Middle East r&lt;/span&gt;egion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience of winning multiple new logo deals&amp;nbsp;of $150k+ ARR and exceeding quota&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A results-oriented mindset&amp;nbsp;with proven ability to conduct effective account/territory planning &amp;amp; pipeline generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sustainable record of signing strategic and large projects, with long and complex sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established sector-related C level contacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful record dealing with strategic buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the relevant key drivers of change in the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working with regional/national/global partners and system integrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior training and experience in value selling and account planning methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility to work in the UK or France.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Ping:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in and facilitate a flexible, collaborative work environment. We’re growing quickly, but remain true to the innovative, can-do startup values that got us here. Most importantly, we keep hiring talented, smart, fun, and genuinely nice people because that’s who we want to succeed with every day.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here are just a few of the things that make Ping special:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company culture that empowers you to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Resource Groups that create a sense of belonging for everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular company and team bonding events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive benefits and perks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global volunteering and community initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO &amp;amp; Holiday Schedule&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progressive Healthcare Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity for Education Reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter Offset (Specific locations)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ping is the collective sum of all our individual experiences, backgrounds and influences and we pride ourselves in growing and learning together. We are committed to building an inclusive and diverse environment where everyone’s individuality is respected and everyone has an Identity. In recruiting for new colleagues, we welcome the unique contributions you can bring and encourage you to be your best self.&lt;/p&gt;
