<p>The successful candidate will engage the SMA and FSHD community to address specific needs, establish and solidify trust and evolve knowledge and care. They will act as key partner working closely with cross-functional stakeholders across geographies, leasing with global functions and supporting EMEA affiliates.</p>
<p>The ideal candidate combines deep rare disease expertise with a strong track record of leading high-impact medical initiatives and engaging effectively with a broad range of stakeholders. They bring experience at both country and regional EMEA level and are comfortable operating in a dynamic, entrepreneurial biotech environment<strong>.</strong></p>
</div><br><strong>Position Responsibilities </strong><br><div>
<ul type="disc">
<li>Co-create the medical strategy, together with the EMEA&nbsp; Medical lead and global medical relevant stakeholders, and drive the execution of EMEA medical plans in alignment with global strategic imperatives.</li>
<li>Develop strong partnerships with the external SMA community, supporting and active participating in key academic, research and/or clinical care forums.</li>
<li>Lead the strategy, development, and execution of key above-market initiatives, including regional advisory boards and preceptorship programs. Act as subject matter expert in medical review processes to support development and localization of EMEA external and field materials</li>
<li>Build and implement engagement and communication plan in partnership with key internal stakeholders (e.g. Global scientific communication teams) t, as well as co-lead with global teams the implementation of associated medical education initiatives when applicable (e.g. medical symposia)</li>
<li>Co-create and define and drive the EMEA RWE strategy in alignment with global priorities and execute EMEA regional evidence generation plans in close partnership with key stakeholders (e.g. Global Evidence Generation Team and Local medical teams). Ensure that RWE collaborations are designed to be fit-for-purpose, uphold the highest standards of scientific and regulatory rigor, and deliver high-quality, credible evidence that supports stakeholders’ requirements</li>
<li>Together with global medical evidence teams, establish and maintain strategic relationships with registry leaders, KOLs, and relevant groups, forging long-term collaborations with academic and data consortia</li>
<li>Oversee initiation and delivery of RWE projects with European/EMEA registry and academic partners, ensuring feasibility, timely execution, and measurable impact</li>
<li>Provide oversight of European/EMEA &nbsp;Investigator-Initiated Studies (IISs) and independent research requests, aligning external research with evidence generation priorities</li>
<li>Facilitates sharing of best practices and knowledge across the organization, supporting the coordination of insights collection and reports</li>

</ul></div><br><strong>Candidate Requirements </strong><br><div>
