<li>Experience in executing medical regional initiatives such as advisory boards and evidence generation projects</li>
<li>Proven track record of success establishing, building and maintaining scientific engagement with influential academic and clinical experts</li>
<li>Knowledge of relevant EU compliance and regulatory guidelines</li>
<li>Ability to summarize complex information and present in a clear, concise, and scientifically accurate manner to a range of audiences</li>
<li>Proven track record of excellent communication and collaboration skills, including recognition by cross-functional partners; work well independently while exhibiting professional maturity, confidence, and competence</li>
