 Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be the first person a merchant contacts when something's not working. This role sits at the center of Tebi's promise to hospitality: when a restaurant reaches out, you turn a stressful moment into a solved one. You'll own the resolution end-to-end, from first reply to final fix, and your fingerprints will be on every process we build to scale support without losing the personal touch.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your day-to-day will be full of merchant communication, investigation and problem solving as well as project work around knowledge base, new tools, AI automation and product updates.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the first response for every Tebi merchant who reaches out, across chat, email, and phone</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diagnose issues fast, using product knowledge and sharp instincts to identify the real problem</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Engineering, Product, and Ops to resolve complex problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hit and beat CSAT, QA, and speed targets in a high-pace environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn what you learn from merchants into documentation, product feedback, and proactive education materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use and set up tools and AI-powered workflows to improve the way you do your work and expand it to company processes</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a creative problem solver who enjoys interacting with hospitality businesses</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are empathetic towards our merchants and curious about their business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, warm communicator who can hold a merchant's confidence through chat, email, and phone</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about the product, want to be an expert in Tebi system and can apply your knowledge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Persistence — you don't let a ticket die in someone else's inbox</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with scheduled on-call time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English and Dutch (is preferred)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Italian and/or Spanish fluency is a strong plus! </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />If this speaks to you we can be the right fit. Learn more about how we work from our Recipe here:<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers"> <u>https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong><br /></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start-up Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible time off</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch in the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team events<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What is Restaurant Software?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurants and other merchants use various software systems such as Point of Sale (POS), Reservations, Kitchen Display Systems (KDS), Payments, Inventory, Staffing, and the list goes on. These systems all need to speak to each other which they frequently don’t. It’s a mess, and we are fixing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From buying a croissant at a cafe to having dinner with friends, it’s a €4 Trillion+ global market and a critical part of everyday life in today's economy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we use AI at Tebi</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use AI the way our merchants use Tebi, to cut out the friction and get to what matters faster. We believe in a world where AI increases quality, efficiency and speed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Tebi, AI isn't a policy or a checkbox, it's just part of how we work. It helps us write, analyse, build, and impro</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tebi/support-specialist-italian-speaking-amsterdam-432853","tags":["Support"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794044417},{"slug":"senior-manager-account-management-amsterdam-232095","company_name":"Datasnipper","title":"Senior Manager Account Management","description":"<h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Account Management is where DataSnipper grows. Our EMEA Accounting AM team manages a book worth tens of millions in ARR across the region's leading audit and accounting firms, and we believe that book can double. The growth won't come from renewals that run themselves. It will come from moving customers onto our AI and Agents platform, defending against cheaper point solutions and free AI tools, and handling firms that keep acquiring each other.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Senior Manager, Account Management – EMEA, you'll lead a team of 5 Account Managers, report to our EMEA Sales leader, and own retention, expansion and forecast accuracy for the region. This is a player-coach role in spirit. You'll be in the deals and in front of senior partners and executives, not managing from a dashboard.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why DataSnipper</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>The best commercial opportunities don't come around every day. Selling technology that's transforming an entire industry is one of them.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe trust is essential to how society works. Every day, we rely on information that's been independently verified, from financial statements to the products we buy, to the sustainability claims companies make. Behind that trust are audit and finance professionals who examine evidence, verify information and hold organizations accountable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At DataSnipper, we build AI solutions that empower those professionals to make those judgements. With Alwin by DataSnipper, our new agentic platform, AI agents now take on end-to-end audit and finance procedures, while every conclusion stays traceable to its source. That frees professionals to focus on the judgment and expertise that make their work so important.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're trusted by Fortune 500 companies, government agencies and all Big Four audit firms. Today, more than <strong>600,000 professionals across 3,000+ organizations in 175 countries</strong> rely on our platform, and in 2025 alone DataSnipper delivered more than <strong>$1.4 billion</strong> in productivity savings to its customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by a $100 million Series B led by Index Ventures, at a $1 billion valuation, we've built a strong foundation for what's next. And as proud members of 1% for the Planet, we care about how we grow, not just how fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>For our commercial teams, this is where things get exciting.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alwin has just launched, demand is growing, and we're expanding into new markets and segments. With a product customers already rely on, there's a huge opportunity to make your mark.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>If you're commercially driven, ambitious, and excited to build something bigger, this is you chance to help shape the future of audit and finance and accelerate your own career along the way.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h2><h3><strong>Lead and Build the Team</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, coach and develop a team of 5 AMs, with hands-on deal coaching on renewal strategy, negotiation and executive engagement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise the talent bar: make the calls on the existing team and hire native speakers for under-covered markets (Dutch, German, French, Spanish)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rebalance books as account loads move from 200 per rep toward 110, so every AM has room to go deep</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Own the Number</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own gross and net revenue retention, expansion and multi-year commitments across the EMEA Accounting book</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring a strategic lens to renewals: move customers up-market on packaging and from legacy products onto our AI platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead high-stakes negotiations with senior partners and executives at Europe's leading accounting firms, including network and multi-entity agreements, price increases, multi-year commitments and competitive displacement threats</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and present business cases that tie DataSnipper to the outcomes partners care about: audit quality, capacity, margin and talent retention. Business conversations, not feature walkthroughs</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Build Forecast Discipline</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a renewal and expansion forecasting method that sees at least a full quarter out (today we see 2 months), ideally run in Gong</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the operating cadence with your team and the CS leaders: renewal reviews, deal rooms and pipeline inspection</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Be the Voice of the EMEA Customer</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Customer Success on adoption and risk, with Product on what customers need from Agents, and with Marketing on firm-level programs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring sharp, data-backed insight on churn risk, competitor activity and pricing pressure to senior leadership</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years in B2B SaaS sales, with at least 2–3 years leading an Account Management or renewals/expansion team (team leads ready to step up are welcome)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of renewing and expanding a product that didn't sell itself. We want commercial operators, not relationship managers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong negotiation skills: you trade concessions for commitments, you don't give too much too early, and you've negotiated directly with economic buyers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Credibility with senior executives: you've had business value conversations with partners, CFOs or managing directors and built business cases with real numbers that won their approval</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep discovery skills: you ask the 2nd, 3rd and 4th question until you reach the real business problem</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A forecasting method you've actually run, and the discipline to inspect it weekly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Urgency and a competitive streak. You'd rather get on a plane to see the customer than send another email</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coachable, and able to coach others. You can name feedback that changed how you work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience moving customers onto AI products is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Audit, accounting or professional services software experience is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English required. Dutch, German, French or Spanish is a strong plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of one of the fastest-growing, profitable unicorn scale-ups in the Netherlands with a global impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity (Stock Appreciation Rights) to share the company's success and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension plan with a 6% contribution on top of your base salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">28 vacation days per year (full-time) to support your work-life balance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work model with at least 3 days onsite in our dynamic Amsterdam office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daily, freshly prepared lunches by our in-house chef to keep you energized</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">NS business card for easy commuting to the office if applicable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to continuous learning and development initiatives to grow your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage with a vibrant international team spread across five global offices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company-wide events like DataSnipper GO, where global teams come together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to a mental health and wellness platform supporting your wellbeing</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Recruitment Process</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruitment Screen (30 minutes, online)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring Manager Interview (30 minutes, online)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assessment Interview (60 minutes, on-site)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final Interview (30 minutes, online)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At DataSnipper, we believe great ideas come from different perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. We are committed to building an inclusive workplace and providing every candidate with a fair and equitable hiring experience.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Our hiring decisions are merit-based and grounded in the skills, experience, potential, and capabilities relevant to the role.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We welcome applicants regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, disability, or any other characteristic that makes you, you.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>What matters to us is what you can bring to the role, the team, and DataSnipper.</em> 🚀</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/datasnipper/senior-manager-account-management-amsterdam-232095","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794033631},{"slug":"staff-software-engineer-alwin-amsterdam-251769","company_name":"Datasnipper","title":"Staff Software Engineer - Alwin","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a <strong>Staff Software Engineer</strong> in our <strong>Amsterdam</strong> office to build <strong>Alwin</strong>, our Agentic Automation Platform for audit and finance, and the systems around it. Alwin agents run multi-step audit procedures over client evidence and return finished workpapers with every number traced back to source. Humans plan, review and sign off.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a <strong>hands-on</strong> role: most of your time will be spent writing code, building the hardest parts of the runtime, prototyping new capabilities and getting them into production. You lead by example: engineers follow your direction because they see it work in your code. Your impact will also come through the engineers and teams you work with.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your mission is to build the best agentic runtime for audit: one that completes audit tasks faster, more accurately, more reliably and at lower cost, while scaling to meet the needs of our largest customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will identify the problems that most constrain that mission, align teams around a technical direction and drive solutions through to measurable results, while building the foundations other engineers use and raising the quality of Alwin’s agents in production.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why DataSnipper?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>The hardest AI problems aren't about getting an answer fast. They're about getting one people can trust.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe trust is essential to how society works. Every day, we rely on information that's been independently verified, from financial statements to the products we buy, to the sustainability claims companies make. Behind that trust are audit and finance professionals who examine evidence, verify information and hold organizations accountable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At DataSnipper, we build AI solutions that empower those professionals. By making evidence easier to trace and verify, we help them focus on the judgment and expertise that make their work so important.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>For our product and engineering team, this is where things get exciting.</strong> In audit, a plausible answer isn't good enough. Every output has to be explainable and traceable back to its source. We've just launched a brand new agentic platform, Alwin by DataSnipper. AI agents running in the cloud across hundreds of documents at once, reasoning across PDF, Word and Excel, with a full audit trail behind every step. There are lots of greenfield problems ahead, and real room to shape what we build and how we build it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And we build at scale. More than <strong>600,000 professionals across 3,000+ organizations in 175 countries</strong> rely on DataSnipper, including Fortune 500 companies, government agencies and all Big Four audit firms. In 2025 alone, the DataSnipper platform delivered more than <strong>$1.4 billion in productivity savings to is customers</strong>. Backed by a $100 million Series B led by Index Ventures, at a $1 billion valuation, and as proud members of 1% for the Planet, we care about how we grow, not just how fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you want to build AI that professionals trust with work that really matters, <em>this is your chance to help shape the future of audit and finance and do the best work of your career along the way.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Will Do:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Results You Will Drive</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Better audit outcomes:</strong> improve how accurately and reliably agents complete real audit tasks, with traceable results and human oversight.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A faster, more efficient runtime:</strong> reduce execution time and cost while scaling to more complex workloads and larger customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>More capable teams:</strong> build foundations and feedback loops that multiple teams use to ship and improve agents faster.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build &amp; Ship</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Write production code every week</strong> on the most complex and critical parts of Alwin</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build proofs of concept</strong> for new agent capabilities, and take the ones that work all the way to production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Champion experimentation and R&amp;D</strong>: try emerging models and techniques, solve hard problems creatively, and turn promising ideas into reliable features</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build shared capabilities that multiple teams adopt</strong>, and remain accountable for whether they make those teams faster and their products more reliable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute directly to the <strong>agent harness</strong> at the core of Alwin: the orchestration, tools, context and evaluation loops every agent runs on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Anticipate where the platform needs to be in 12 to 18 months, and make design decisions now that minimize the cost of future change</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Agents in Production</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build <strong>agents that are reliable in a regulated domain</strong>: grounding, evaluation before release, human-in-the-loop, traceability of every action</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve how teams build Alwin</strong> by establishing tooling and feedback loops that help them detect agent failures, prioritize improvements, prevent regressions and ship production-ready agents faster</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Jump into the hardest incidents across teams</strong>, resolve immediate problems and turn what you learn into lasting, systemic fixes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make the trade-offs between model cost, latency and accuracy explicit, and measure them in production</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead by Example</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own ambiguous, high-impact technical problems across teams</strong>: define the problem, align on the trade-offs and prove the solution in code</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Set the standard</strong> for code quality, testing and security through your own code and reviews, aligned with <strong>OWASP GenAI</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive AI-assisted engineering by example</strong>: try new tools, show what works and help teams adopt them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mentor senior engineers and grow future staff engineers</strong> by pairing, reviewing and building alongside them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Product to spot opportunities and differentiators against the competition, and shape the roadmap with what you have proven is possible</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You Bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>10+ years</strong> in software engineering, with strong, production-grade <strong>Python</strong>, and you still write a lot of code</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep hands-on experience <strong>building and shipping agentic or LLM systems in production yourself</strong> (control loops, tool calling, context engineering and evaluation), with evidence that your work improved quality, reliability, speed, cost or scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of <strong>personally solving ambiguous, high-impact problems across teams</strong>. Your work delivered measurable results and produced systems or practices that others adopted</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience <strong>mentoring senior engineers</strong> and growing technical leadership beyond your own team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong fundamentals in <strong>distributed systems</strong>, <strong>software architecture</strong> and <strong>data modeling</strong> on a major <strong>cloud platform</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with <strong>security, access control and auditability</strong> for enterprise or regulated customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product sense</strong>: you know which technical bets matter for customers and the business, and have influenced product and engineering direction through evidence and clear trade-offs, without relying on formal authority</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficient with <strong>AI-assisted engineering</strong>, and experience driving its adoption beyond your own work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written and verbal communication, across time zones and with technical and non-technical audiences</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building <strong>platforms</strong> that other teams and customers build on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Multi-agent orchestration</strong> or durable, long-running workflows at scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Retrieval and knowledge systems</strong>, or <strong>document processing</strong> (OCR, classification, structured extraction)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with <strong>Forward Deployed Engineers, Solution Architects and GTM teams</strong> on enterprise rollouts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience at a <strong>scale-up</strong> going through rapid growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Domain experience in <strong>audit, accounting or fintech</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of one of the fastest-growing, profitable unicorn scale-ups in the Netherlands with a global impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity (Stock Appreciation Rights) to share the company's success and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension plan with a 6% contribution on top of your base salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">28 vacation days per year (full-time) to support your work-life balance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work model with at least 3 days onsite in our dynamic Amsterdam office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daily, freshly prepared lunches by our in-house chef to keep you energized</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">NS business card for easy commuting to the office if applicable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to continuous learning and development initiatives to grow your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage with a vibrant international team spread across five global offices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company-wide events like DataSnipper GO, where global teams come together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to a mental health and wellness platform supporting your wellbeing</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Recruitment Process</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruitment Screen (30 minutes, online)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring Manager Interview (30 minutes, online)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Live coding Interview (75 minutes, online)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">System design interview (60 minutes, on-site)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final Interview (30 minutes, online)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>At DataSnipper, we believe great ideas come from different perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. We are committed to building an inclusive workplace and providing every candidate with a fair and equitable hiring experience.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Our hiring decisions are merit-based and grounded in the skills, experience, potential, and capabilities relevant to the role.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We welcome applicants regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, disability, or any other characteristic that makes you, you.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>What matters to us is what you can bring to the role, the team, and DataSnipper.</em> 🚀</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/datasnipper/staff-software-engineer-alwin-amsterdam-251769","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794033631},{"slug":"remote-senior-staff-platform-engineer-382004","company_name":"Duna","title":"(Senior/Staff) Platform Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At Duna, we see the company as the second product we're building and are continually working to create a transparent, ambitious culture. We want this to be the place where you do your best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission is to redefine identity for the global economy. We're backed by world-class investors including CapitalG and Index Ventures, as well as founders and executives from companies like Stripe, Adyen, Notion, Remote, Qonto, Framer, Anthropic, Mollie, OpenAI and Goldman Sachs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Duna's infrastructure is part of the product. Enterprise customers buy our reliability, security posture and auditability, not just our features.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT YOU'LL BE DOING IN THIS ROLE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and evolve our cloud platform: AWS, Kubernetes, networking, Terraform, CI/CD and observability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape how our engineers build and ship, from local setups and preview environments to deploys, so the safe path is also the fast one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead incidents calmly, find the root cause and make sure the fix holds</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn recurring manual work into automation and self-service tools that engineers actually use</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help the team run AI agents in engineering safely, with the sandboxes and guardrails that make it possible</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior experience as a platform, DevOps, site reliability, infrastructure or cloud engineer. The title matters less than what you have built and run</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depth in cloud infrastructure: Kubernetes, networking and infrastructure as code in production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience improving developer experience is a strong plus, and an interest in security or observability is a welcome extra</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time at a startup or scale-up, where you owned problems from start to finish</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence to make calls, explain them clearly and push back when something looks wrong</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity across clouds and tools. We care more about how quickly you learn than which provider you know best</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in regulated environments such as fintech, payments or identity is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our platform runs on AWS and Kubernetes with Terraform, Postgres and RabbitMQ, alongside a Node.js and TypeScript product stack built on event sourcing. You will not have used all of it before. We care more about the depth you bring and how you pick up the rest.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A final note before you apply: please read through our website in detail. You'll find the fundamentals there: what we believe in, how we work, and why we're building this company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a remote-first, fast-moving team of builders looking for exceptional people who love to create, build, and ship. Beyond passion and grit, we highly value curiosity, authenticity and kindness.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like you, we'd love to hear from you!<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>PS. We are looking to hire passionate people from a variety of backgrounds. So even if you don't check all the boxes, we welcome your application!</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/duna/remote-senior-staff-platform-engineer-382004","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1794033631},{"slug":"brand-web-designer-amsterdam-379352","company_name":"Feedbackfruits","title":"Brand & Web Designer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi, I'm <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rosa-mauleon/">Rosa</a>, Head of Brand at FeedbackFruits. 👋</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As FeedbackFruits evolves, so does the role design plays in how we build and communicate our brand. Campaigns and marketing materials will always be part of the picture, but we're putting a much bigger focus on our website, our digital experiences and the brand systems that help us do better work, more consistently.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">I'm looking for a brand designer with a strong B2B marketing background, someone who combines excellent visual craft with real, hands-on website experience. You'll help evolve our visual identity, develop creative concepts for campaigns and launches, and bring that work to life on our website and landing pages, from the first layout to the moment a page goes live.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The first project you'd pick up with me is one I'm particularly excited about: evolving our brand so it sits closer to the new visual language of our product. After that, you'll take ownership of our website and landing pages, shaping the direction together with me while owning the design and execution, and you'll make sure our brand shows up consistently wherever people come across us, from a launch campaign to an ebook.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Beyond the design itself, I'm looking for someone who takes real ownership: someone who asks the right questions before jumping into a brief, spots what could be better and isn't afraid to challenge the obvious solution. We also use AI a lot at FeedbackFruits, and I'd love you to bring that same mindset to design, building templates and systems that help the whole team create on-brand work without starting from scratch every time. You'll have a real say in our creative direction, and as the team grows, there's room for you to grow with it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evolve our brand identity and translate it into a distinctive, coherent visual language across our website, campaigns and marketing materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and improve our marketing website and landing pages, from early concepts and layouts to responsive designs, and build and maintain pages yourself</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop creative concepts for campaigns and product launches, and carry them through to ads, social, ebooks, brochures, presentations and event materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create hero and product visuals that make a complex product clear and compelling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make our website clearer, more engaging and easier to navigate, with an eye on accessibility and conversion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build reusable components, templates and guidelines so colleagues can create on-brand materials themselves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring structure to how design work gets requested, briefed, reviewed and delivered, and find ways for AI and automation to take repetitive work off the team's plate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Brief and work with external specialists in development, motion, video or illustration when a project needs extra expertise</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have around 3–5 years of experience as a brand or marketing designer, ideally at a B2B tech or SaaS company, or at an agency working with B2B clients</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your portfolio shows real breadth in B2B marketing design: landing pages, ads, brochures, ebooks, hero visuals and product visuals. You know how to make a complex product easy to understand and good to look at</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Website work is a regular part of your job, not an occasional task. You've designed and built marketing pages yourself and can explain what you owned. You work in Webflow, our platform, or in something comparable like Framer and are happy to switch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think in concepts, not just layouts, and you have a strong eye for typography, composition and hierarchy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can take a project from a fuzzy brief to delivery without someone managing it for you, and you keep a clear head about priorities when several people need something from you at once</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand what design needs to do for marketing, and you can explain your choices to non-designers in a way that brings them along</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You look for ways to work smarter, whether that's a template, a component or an AI workflow that saves the team hours</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're confident in Figma and communicate well in English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You live within commuting distance of Amsterdam and are available 38 hours per week, with at least 2 days a week from our Amsterdam office</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you get:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 paid holidays per year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work schedule (2 days onsite)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A day off for your birthday</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advantageous pension scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3 days of volunteering leave per year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">€550 Learning &amp; Development budget per year + 3 days paid leave for learning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel allowance and Swapfiets subscription</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free access to our office gym</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited access to mental health support via OpenUp</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: €65K – €70K</p><ul><li> • Estimaded gross yearly salary, including 8% holiday allowance €65K – €70K</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/feedbackfruits/brand-web-designer-amsterdam-379352","tags":["Go To Market"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794033631},{"slug":"bookkeeper-boekhouder-amsterdam-486782","company_name":"Monumental","title":"Bookkeeper (Boekhouder)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Monumental is automating on-site construction with robotics and software. Our mission is to make construction software-defined and autonomous - a future where beautiful, bespoke buildings go up in a single day, with minimal labour.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a growing team of engineers, operators and technicians from diverse backgrounds, including consumer tech, finance and media, and companies like Dyson, Shopify, Meta and Tesla. It's still the early days of building the company, and this is a chance to make an outsized impact on a problem that matters. From day one, you'll be working with an experienced founding team, backed by a $32M Series B led by Khosla Ventures and Plural, alongside other renowned investors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monumental is based in the city centre of Amsterdam, in a beautiful facility with a fully equipped workshop and robot testing floor. We build the whole stack in-house, hardware and software. Our work involves building robots in our workshop and houses on real construction sites, so we're onsite five days a week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Read more on why we believe you should spend your time working on construction, and learn about <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.monumental.co/our-vision/">our vision</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.monumental.co/about/">company</a>. You might enjoy our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/@buildmonumental">YouTube Channel</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2-Q2F0Fcx4A">Based in Europe’s film on how we’re fixing Europe’s housing shortage</a>, or <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DOo8n19XEns">this video by Andreas Klinger of what our office looks like</a>.</p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Bookkeeper to bring our day-to-day bookkeeping and month-end close in-house. You'll be our first dedicated bookkeeper, taking over from our external accounting firm and running the books for our growing group: five Dutch BVs today, plus our entities abroad.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our transaction volume has roughly doubled this year, and 2027 is the first financial year our accounts will be audited. You'll own the reconciliations, records and close process that make our numbers reliable, working closely with our finance lead, purchasing team and external accountants. The external accountants will continue to handle annual accounts and corporate tax, with local advisors handling tax filings abroad.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on bookkeeping role for someone with at least three years of experience running the full cycle through month-end. Our data and processes need cleaning up. If you enjoy turning a messy administration into a tidy one, this is that job. As you settle in, there is room to take on VAT filing and monthly payroll processing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role is based at our Amsterdam HQ, on-site five days a week. Salary is up to €50,000 gross a year, including the 8% holiday allowance.</p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own daily bookkeeping.</strong> Code supplier invoices and card spend in Spendesk with the right GL account, VAT code and cost centre, and post them to the general ledger without re-keying. Keep supplier records clean and prepare payment runs. Supplier bank-detail changes are independently verified and approved; payment approval and release sit with the finance lead.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep accounts reconciled.</strong> Reconcile bank accounts, keep payables and receivables current, and investigate outstanding items so every balance is supported or explained.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run the month-end close.</strong> Close all entities to a fixed timetable, initially by working day eight and moving towards working day five. Own accruals, prepayments and balance-sheet reconciliations, collect or prepare foreign entities' figures, agree intercompany balances and reconcile group reporting to the ledgers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Maintain fixed assets and inventory records.</strong> Keep the fixed-asset register up to date, including capitalisation and depreciation of our robot fleet under agreed accounting policies, and reconcile inventory accounts to month-end stock values.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prepare Dutch VAT returns.</strong> Prepare quarterly btw returns with our external accountants reviewing, and take over filing them over time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep the books audit-ready.</strong> Maintain supporting schedules and an audit file throughout the year. Be a day-to-day contact for our external accountants and support the audit of our 2027 accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve how we work.</strong> Document the close, fix recurring errors and use spreadsheets, software and AI tools to reduce manual work while checking the results carefully. Depending on your experience, take on payroll processing in Loket over time, with payroll tax filings remaining with our external accountants.</p></li></ul><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Full-cycle bookkeeping experience.</strong> You have at least three years of experience running the books through month-end, at an accounting firm (accountantskantoor) or in-house.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on Dutch VAT experience.</strong> You've prepared Dutch btw returns and can work through the supporting records.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong reconciliation skills.</strong> You've handled balance-sheet reconciliations, accruals and prepayments, beyond processing invoices. You investigate differences and follow them through to a resolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accuracy and ownership.</strong> You keep records organised, meet close deadlines and raise missing information or accounting questions early. You'd rather find the €12 difference than book it to suspense.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fluent English and professional working Dutch.</strong> English is our working language, and your manager doesn't speak Dutch. You can independently read and process Dutch invoices, tax correspondence and payroll documents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfort with systems and confidential information.</strong> You work confidently with spreadsheets, learn new accounting tools and handle financial and employee information carefully.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Nice to have: Twinfield, Basecone or Spendesk (Exact, Odoo or similar also counts); multi-entity or multi-country bookkeeping, intercompany and consolidation; fixed-asset or inventory accounting in hardware or manufacturing; statutory audit support; Dutch payroll experience, ideally in Loket; an accounting qualification such as MBO-4/HBO, SPD or Praktijkdiploma Boekhouden; experience automating repetitive work.</em></p></li></ul><h2>Why Monumental?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining Monumental means being at the forefront of a movement aimed at making significant strides in the construction industry. Here, your work has the potential to impact not just the company but the future of how we build. If you're driven by innovation, eager to tackle complex challenges, and ready to make a tangible difference, we want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For open applications (where you don't see an exact role match), please reach out to us at: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- - share with us the most interesting or challenging project you've worked on, why you want to join and your CV or portfolio.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unfortunately we do not currently support internships.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don't meet all the qualifications here but are excited about Monumental and feel you'd still be able to help us tackle complex challenges, do get in touch. We welcome generalists who focus on outcomes and are eager to learn on the job.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/monumental/bookkeeper-boekhouder-amsterdam-486782","tags":["Company Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794033631},{"slug":"senior-manager-global-access-amsterdam-216533","company_name":"Mytomorrows","title":"Senior Manager, Global Access","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About myTomorrows</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">myTomorrows is a global health tech company dedicated to breaking down barriers for patients seeking treatment options.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We strive to enable earlier and better treatment access by bridging the gap between those searching for possible options, and the companies who develop them. We work closely with patients, healthcare professionals, trial sites, patient advocacy groups, and BioPharma – connecting key stakeholders in the drug development ecosystem.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve developed a cutting-edge AI-powered technology platform that simplifies and streamlines access to drugs in development. To support our users and clients, we have a range of industry-expert specialized teams ready to help. Our services include clinical trial patient recruitment, Expanded Access Program management and Real-World Data collection.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With a global footprint spanning 134 countries, to date we’ve supported over 17,000 patients, 3,000 physicians and 350 sites, earning the trust of 60+ BioPharma companies. In October 2025, we closed a €25M investment with Avego Healthcare Capital to fuel our global ambitions and scale the business.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of treatment access - making tomorrow’s therapies accessible for people who need them today. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vendor Management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the primary point of contact for all external vendors collaborating with myTomorrows within the Global Access function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support procurement efforts during vendor RFP processes, including requirements scoping, proposal evaluation, selection, and contracting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the quality and legal team during vendor onboarding and ongoing maintenance, ensuring all documentation, SOPs, and compliance records are accurate and up to date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct structured regular check-ins with vendors to monitor performance, track program milestones, and resolve operational issues in a timely manner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support procurement effort during annual vendor reviews</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner Sourcing &amp; Network Expansion</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively identify and engage new global partners to expand myTomorrows' reach across both free-of-charge and paid expanded access programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain a pipeline of potential partners across key geographic markets, with attention to regulatory and operational feasibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the partnership terms negotiation and agreements in alignment with internal legal and compliance requirements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>EAP Operations Support</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with the Operations team to support the delivery of paid EAP programs, contributing subject matter expertise throughout the program lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply proven strategies to accelerate reimbursement timelines and identify funding opportunities that support program sustainability and growth.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Legal, Finance, Regulatory, and Operations stakeholders to ensure vendor and partner activities remain compliant and aligned with organizational objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of internal processes, frameworks, and tools related to vendor governance and access program management.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications &amp; Experience</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's degree in Life Sciences, Business, Healthcare Management, or a related field; advanced degree preferred.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimum 5 years of experience in the pharmaceutical, biotech, or healthcare industry, with solid experience in (paid) Expanded Access Programs or early access/compassionate use programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience managing external vendor and partner relationships at a global scale, including RFP processes, contracting, and performance oversight.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with reimbursement pathways and funding mechanisms, preferably in oncology, rare diseases, or specialty therapeutics.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skills &amp; Competencies</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong vendor governance skills, including the ability to manage complex multi-vendor environments across multiple geographies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of global regulatory and compliance requirements applicable to (paid) expanded access programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder management and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build effective relationships with external partners and internal teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High degree of organizational capability, with the ability to manage multiple programs simultaneously while maintaining attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear and professional written and verbal communication skills.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of the regulatory landscape governing (paid) expanded access and compassionate use programs across key markets (e.g., EU, US, APAC).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience negotiating with payers, including familiarity with reimbursement frameworks, funding discussions, and access-related pricing considerations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience sourcing and scaling partner networks across multiple international markets.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal opportunities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">myTomorrows is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, beyond upholding discrimination-free practices, we are committed to cultivating a workplace where difference and diversity are protected and celebrated. The best work comes from our best selves, and we go to great lengths in supporting our team members to be just that. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/mytomorrows/senior-manager-global-access-amsterdam-216533","tags":["CEO Office"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam HQ","created_at":1794033631},{"slug":"process-safety-lead-amsterdam-242270","company_name":"Skynrg","title":"Process Safety Lead","description":"<h1><strong>About the role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As SkyNRG grows, we are looking for a Process Safety Lead to build and embed our corporate Process Safety Management framework.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will set the standards for how process safety is managed across our projects and future assets, from design and construction through commissioning and operations. Working across Engineering, Projects, Operations and HSE, you will combine technical expertise with functional leadership to strengthen process safety across the organization.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your key responsibilities include:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and implement SkyNRG’s corporate Process Safety Management (PSM) framework as part of the Integrated Management System.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish and embed process safety standards and procedures across current and future projects, including construction, commissioning, start-up and operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure compliance with SEVESO III requirements and support the Major Accident Prevention Policy, Safety Reports, regulatory inspections and audits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Govern key process safety activities, including HAZOP, LOPA, QRA and Management of Change (MOC).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and monitor process safety KPIs and barrier management to strengthen risk control and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead process safety audits, incident learning and improvement initiatives across projects and assets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build process safety capability across the organization through training, guidance and functional leadership for Engineering, Projects, Operations, Maintenance and contractors.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a growing company in a rapidly evolving industry, we are looking for people who embrace change and are motivated to actively contribute to building and scaling our business. You are someone who feels comfortable in an entrepreneurial environment, takes ownership, and thrives when things are still developing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine deep technical expertise with the ability to turn complex regulatory and risk-management requirements into practical standards. Structured and strategic in your approach, you are also willing to work hands-on to move implementation forward. You communicate clearly, make risk-based decisions, and can influence senior stakeholders without relying on formal authority.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You recognize yourself in the following:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A master’s degree in Chemical Engineering, Process Engineering, Process Safety, or a closely related technical discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least five years of relevant process safety experience within oil and gas, renewable fuels, chemicals, or another major hazard environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical knowledge of SEVESO III requirements and their application within Major Accident Hazard facilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience developing or implementing Process Safety Management frameworks, Integrated Management Systems, or corporate process safety standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical expertise in HAZOP, LOPA, QRA, Management of Change, Mechanical Integrity, contractor management, and commissioning or start-up activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience assessing, governing, or assuring hazard studies across projects or operational environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven ability to design and deliver process safety training for multidisciplinary audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong incident investigation skills, with the ability to translate findings into organizational learning and sustainable improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to influence stakeholders across Engineering, Projects, Operations, Maintenance, and site leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional fluency in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with digital risk-assessment or barrier-management tools would be an advantage. A recognized qualification such as MoSHE, NEBOSH Process Safety, or an equivalent certification is also beneficial. Direct experience engaging with regulators or contributing to SEVESO Safety Reports would make your profile particularly relevant.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About SkyNRG</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2009, SkyNRG has been a change maker in the aviation industry. We are dedicated to supplying and producing high-integrity Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), making sustainable aviation a reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaboration is fundamental to achieving our ambition. We nurture genuine relationships with global partners in our drive to make SAF <em>the</em> alternative to fossil jet fuel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our in-house team of SAF experts have helped over 60 airlines and corporates reduce their climate impact using the Book &amp; Claim mechanism; the most transparent and traceable way to support aviation sustainability with real emission reductions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sustainability is woven into the fabric of our company. We maintain an independent Sustainability Board, which advises the company on feedstocks and provides strategic guidance on wide-ranging sustainability issues. SkyNRG operations are certified against the RSB EU RED, CORSIA, and Book &amp; Claim standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At SkyNRG, you’ll find:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An innovation-driven culture – where big ideas turn into real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth opportunities – in a fast-scaling, industry-changing company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative team – where your ideas and expertise are valued</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A mission that matters – leading the change in the energy transition by producing and supplying high-integrity SAF</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What we offer</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a brand-new office in the heart of Amsterdam, designed for collaboration and creativity. Most importantly, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to a truly game-changing green initiative, making a real impact on the aviation industry and the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Besides that, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 paid holidays + 2 for choosing sustainable travel options for your holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to a sustainable organization (B Corp)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attractive bonus scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">€5.000,- dedicated budget every 3 years for professional development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commuting travel reimbursement + Lease a Bike plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An office in the city centre of Amsterdam (Nieuwmarkt)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work where it feels best for you: we offer flexible (hybrid in-office) working arrangements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous employer pension contribution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid Volunteering Day</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to our electric company boat (also available for private use), free lunch, and lots of social activities – all part of the deal!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Is this you?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to take the next step in your career with SkyNRG? Explore our vacancies and become part of our company of change makers. Together, we can change the future of flying.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information about SkyNRG visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.skynrg.com"><u>www.skynrg.com</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>📌 Please note: We do not accept sales inquiries or intermediary services.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At SkyNRG, we deeply value inclusion and diversity. As an equal opportunity employer, we are dedicated to ensuring every applicant has a fair chance, irrespective of race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, or any other legally protected characteristics.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skynrg/process-safety-lead-amsterdam-242270","tags":["COO Organisation"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794033630},{"slug":"accounts-payable-specialist-capelle-a-d-ijssel-388729","company_name":"I3D","title":"Accounts Payable Specialist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://i3D.net">i3D.net</a>, we provide world-class global coverage with one of the <strong>most interconnected networks</strong> in the world. Our solutions focus on low latency, zero packet loss, and unmatched scalability, enabling seamless experiences for millions of users worldwide. With dedicated support, bespoke solutions, and cutting-edge technology, we